comments[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-15T10:38:43.585Z","harness:codex","Duplicate-check evidence 2026-08-15: all-status searches for history-author-acknowledge,--all-actionable,dry-run,preview,zero selection,and the GitHub issue number found no item with this exact command-path defect. pm-h90s owns the completed acknowledgement feature,pm-jwmszf owns completed recovery discoverability,pm-tobi records the destructive-safety decision,and open pm-kexu covers update-many preview rather than this immutable-history command; all are linked as provenance,not duplicated or reopened."
  "2026-08-15T10:41:57.231Z","harness:codex","GitHub linkage evidence 2026-08-15: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1028#issuecomment-5301855572 points GitHub #1028 to this canonical PM item and summarizes the SDK-native preview/apply and zero-selection contract."
body: "## Safety contract\n\nThe preview and apply paths must share the exact same selector implementation. Preview returns the prospective immutable acknowledgement coordinates, counts, omissions, and recovery/apply command but writes no item, workspace, or history state. Apply records normal provenance and remains auditable.\n\n## Empty-selection contract\n\nZero actionable coordinates is a successful, truthful no-op unless the caller selected a strict mode that explicitly makes no-match an error. The output must distinguish no match from malformed input, tracker corruption, and already-acknowledged coordinates.\n\n## Scope\n\nThis is specific to history-author-acknowledge. It complements the broader update-many preview work but does not depend on it and must not be folded into a generic destructive-command rewrite."
